From 1073cb553a66f53e71554af756785d1817e53d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Navi48-MacOS contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:14:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] radv: Darwin: pick the canned device from the kext's GC
 version (Navi 33 / gfx1102)

The Darwin backend always answered device-info queries from the canned
gfx1201 (Navi 48) entry.  The kext reports its GC version in QueryInfo, so
the handshake now picks the drm-shim entry from it: 12.0.1 -> "gfx1201",
11.0.2 -> "navi33" (RX 7600, device 0x7480, the entry Mesa already ships).
GB_ADDR_CONFIG (from QueryInfo, ReadRegs as the fallback, as 0007 does) is
checked against the chosen entry's own recorded value instead of the gfx1201
constant.  The marketing name follows the device too (7480 -> "AMD Radeon
RX 7600").  RADV_DARWIN_CANNED=<name> overrides the choice (and picks the
entry for the RADV_DARWIN_HOST_BO stand-in, default gfx1201).
RADV_DARWIN_MOCK_N33=1 makes the mock answer as the RX 7600 kext (GC 11.0.2,
GB_ADDR_CONFIG 0x343).  The PRT half-VA reservation stays: Linux uses it for
gfx11 too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
